---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";

/*
 * Every statement on this page maps to something the 1.0 app does (App Store
 * audit 2026-10-07, F-14). Before adding a claim, find the code path that
 * implements it; before removing a feature, remove its line here.
 *
 *   Report paths      covey-ios PublicProfileView "Report profile",
 *                     PlanDetailView "Report plan", PlanChatView and
 *                     ChatThreadView "Report message", ChatThreadView
 *                     "Report user", CoveyDetailView "Report Covey",
 *                     FeedPostCard "Report recap", PlaceDetailView
 *                     "Report place"
 *   24-hour review    public.safety_policy (served to both clients)
 *   Blocking          block_user; blocked senders hidden in plan and group chats
 *   Automated checks  Gemini text and image checks; high risk is hidden
 *                     automatically and queued for a person
 *   21+ drinks        plan minimum-age rule for alcohol-centred plans
 *   Appeals           SuspendedView's "Appeal" opens this page (AppRouter)
 */
const lastUpdated = "October 15, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Safety"
  description="How Covey keeps plans safe: in-app reporting, human review within 24 hours, blocking, automated checks, and what happens to people who break the rules."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-[var(--section-y)]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Safety</div>
    <h1 class="display t-h1 mb-4">Safety at Covey</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-ink-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] mb-12">
      Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div class="card p-6 mb-12">
      <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        Covey is built for people making plans in the real world. We have zero
        tolerance for objectionable content and abusive behavior: content that
        breaks our rules is removed, and the people who post it are suspended
        or banned.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Who Covey is for</h2>
        <p>
          Covey is for adults 18 and over. Plans built around drinks are open
          only to people 21 and over, and a host can't lower that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Community expectations</h2>
        <p>
          Treat people with respect. Do not harass, threaten, discriminate,
          impersonate others, share private information without consent, post
          sexual or violent content, spam people, or use Covey to coordinate
          illegal or dangerous activity. The full rules are the Acceptable Use
          Policy in our
          <a href="/terms" class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">Terms of Service</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Report something in the app</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">Every report is read by a person on our team. You can report:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>a person, with <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report profile</strong> on their profile, or <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report user</strong> in a chat;</li>
          <li>a message, by pressing and holding it and choosing <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report message</strong>;</li>
          <li>a plan, with <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report plan</strong> on the plan;</li>
          <li>a Covey, with <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report Covey</strong> on the Covey's page;</li>
          <li>a recap, with <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report recap</strong> in its menu;</li>
          <li>a place, with <strong class="text-ink font-medium">Report place</strong> on the place.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Pick a reason and add anything that helps us understand what
          happened. If you can't report from the app, email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.safety}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">{SITE.emails.safety}</a>
          and name the account, plan or message involved.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">What happens next</h2>
        <p>
          We review every report within 24 hours. Reports involving an
          immediate risk to someone's safety go to the front of the queue. When
          something breaks our rules, we remove it and suspend or permanently
          ban the account responsible. A suspended account can't message, post,
          create plans or invite anyone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Blocking</h2>
        <p>
          Block someone from their profile or from a chat. They can't message
          you, send you a friend request or invite you, and they aren't told.
          Their messages are hidden from you, including in plan and group chats
          you're both in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Automated checks</h2>
        <p>
          Profiles, plans, Coveys, recaps, messages and photos are checked
          automatically for content that breaks our rules. Anything flagged as
          high risk is hidden straight away and sent to a person, who decides
          whether it stays down. A check never suspends or bans anyone on its
          own. Section 8 of our
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">Privacy Policy</a>
          explains how these checks work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="appeals">
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Appeals</h2>
        <p>
          If your content was removed or your account was suspended and you
          think we got it wrong, email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.support}?subject=Appeal`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">{SITE.emails.support}</a>
          with "Appeal" in the subject, from the email address on your account.
          Someone who wasn't involved in the original decision will review it.
          You can still report other people while your account is suspended.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Before you meet</h2>
        <p>
          Meet in a public place the first time, tell a friend where you're
          going, get yourself there and back, and never send money to someone
          you met on Covey. Covey doesn't run background checks on anyone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">Emergencies</h2>
        <p>
          Covey is not an emergency service. If you or someone else is in
          immediate danger, call 911 first. For non-emergency help with an
          account or plan, email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.support}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">{SITE.emails.support}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
